    "atdd_status_md": "## Adversarial TDD Status\nFeature: striped-block-cache\nMode: greenfield\nMax rounds: 3\nCurrent round: 3\nStatus: complete\nSubstage: complete\n\n## Round History\n| Round | Analyst vectors | Breaker tests | Confirmed bugs | Theoretical | Status |\n|-------|----------------|---------------|----------------|-------------|--------|\n| 1     | 20             | 38            | 1              | 2           | complete |\n| 2     | 7              | 10            | 0              | 2           | complete |\n| 3     | 4              | 7             | 2              | 1           | complete |\n",
    "known_issues_md": "# Known Issues \u2014 striped-block-cache\n<!-- Maintained by Spec Analyst. Do not edit manually. -->\n\n## Resolved patterns\n<!-- RESOLVED entries: confirmed bugs and their fix patterns -->\n\n### RESOLVED-1 (Round 1): Builder sentinel collision\n**Bug:** Builder used `shardCount = -1` as both \"not set\" sentinel and accepted\nnegative user input. Calling `.shardCount(-1)` was silently treated as \"use default\"\ninstead of throwing IllegalArgumentException.\n**Fix pattern:** Added explicit `shardCountSet` boolean flag to distinguish \"not set\"\nfrom \"explicitly set to a value\".\n**Test:** `StripedBlockCacheTest.builderRejectsNegativeShardCount()`\n\n### RESOLVED-2 (Round 3): LruBlockCache capacity overflow\n**Bug:** `LruBlockCache` accepted `long capacity` but `LinkedHashMap.size()`\nreturns `int`. When capacity > `Integer.MAX_VALUE`, the eviction callback\n`size() > cap` was always false \u2014 eviction never triggered. Reachable via\n`StripedBlockCache.builder().totalCapacity((long)Integer.MAX_VALUE + 2).shardCount(1)`.\n**Fix pattern:** Added `capacity > Integer.MAX_VALUE` validation in\n`LruBlockCache.Builder.build()`. StripedBlockCache protected transitively.\n**Tests:** `capacityExceedingIntMaxBreaksEviction()`,\n`stripedCacheRejectsPerShardCapacityExceedingIntMax()`\n\n## Tendencies\n<!-- TENDENCY entries: recurring implementation anti-patterns -->\n\n### TENDENCY-2: API type width mismatch\nPublic API accepts `long` but internal data structure uses `int`. The\n`LruBlockCache(long capacity)` / `LinkedHashMap.size() \u2192 int` mismatch was\nthe root cause of RESOLVED-2. Watch for similar mismatches whenever a public\nAPI accepts a wider type than the backing implementation supports.\n\n### TENDENCY-1: Sentinel value collisions\nThe Implementer's first pass used a magic sentinel value (-1) that overlapped with\nvalid domain input. Watch for this pattern in any builder or configuration object.\n\n## Watch items\n<!-- WATCH entries: unverified risks requiring monitoring -->\n\n### WATCH-1: Integer division capacity loss\n`totalCapacity / shardCount` truncates. With totalCapacity=7, shardCount=4, each\nshard gets capacity 1 \u2192 actual usable capacity is 4, not 7. `capacity()` reports 7.\nThis is by design (work-plan contract) but could confuse consumers. Test\n`integerDivisionCapacityLoss` documents the behaviour.\n\n### WATCH-2: size() consistency under concurrent modification (Round 1)\n`size()` sums across shards without a global lock, so the returned value may be\nslightly stale under concurrent modification. Tests confirm it doesn't throw or\ndeadlock, but the value is a best-effort snapshot, not a consistent point-in-time\nread. This is acceptable per the work-plan contract.\n\n### WATCH-3: getOrLoad stampede (Round 2)\nThe default `BlockCache.getOrLoad` is not stampede-proof. Under concurrent\nmisses for the same key, the loader may be called multiple times. This is by\ndesign (interface default, not overridden). Test\n`getOrLoadStampedeDoesNotCorrupt` documents the behaviour. If stampede\nprotection becomes a requirement, the method must be overridden in\nStripedBlockCache with a per-key lock or similar mechanism.\n",
    "gaps_md": ""
